  "longest_interventions": [
    {
      "rank": 1,
      "member_code": "Charlie-McConalogue.D.2011-03-09",
      "full_name": "Charlie McConalogue",
      "speech_id": "speech:19341339f777d0ef26d99a59",
      "debate_date": "2026-04-15",
      "speech_order": "470",
      "word_count": 5173,
      "classification_status": "classified",
      "text_preview": "I very much welcome the opportunity to address the House this evening on matters relating to football, the most popular team sport in Ireland. Football can take us from the absolute peaks of delight, such as when Troy Pa"
    },
    {
      "rank": 2,
      "member_code": "Paschal-Donohoe.S.2007-07-23",
      "full_name": "Paschal Donohoe",
      "speech_id": "speech:f1fe03907cef2b8f3fc73dbf",
      "debate_date": "2025-10-07",
      "speech_order": "1",
      "word_count": 4828,
      "classification_status": "classified",
      "text_preview": "Introduction Budget 2026 will invest in our future while securing the jobs, prosperity and stability of today. It will tackle the serious challenges of meeting our housing and investment needs. At the same time, we are p"
    },
    {
      "rank": 3,
      "member_code": "Kieran-O'Donnell.D.2007-06-14",
      "full_name": "Kieran O'Donnell",
      "speech_id": "speech:ae6555d7d7ba80143940cd23",
      "debate_date": "2025-06-12",
      "speech_order": "305",
      "word_count": 4748,
      "classification_status": "classified",
      "text_preview": "I welcome the opportunity to discuss nursing homes and the care of older people. To begin, I want to acknowledge the \"RTÉ Investigates\" programme that was broadcast on 4 June. This was a very hard-hitting and harrowing p"
    },
    {
      "rank": 4,
      "member_code": "Jennifer-Carroll-MacNeill.D.2020-02-08",
      "full_name": "Jennifer Carroll MacNeill",
      "speech_id": "speech:8ab7f7d8bde7935d42214e5c",
      "debate_date": "2025-02-26",
      "speech_order": "415",
      "word_count": 4528,
      "classification_status": "classified",
      "text_preview": "I thank an Cathaoirleach Gníomhach for making the time for these statements, which I believe are the first on health in this new Dáil. The Government and I are fully committed to a vision of a universal health and social"
    },
    {
      "rank": 5,
      "member_code": "Simon-Harris.D.2011-03-09",
      "full_name": "Simon Harris",
      "speech_id": "speech:5b6e673e64250f37e3c44f8d",
      "debate_date": "2025-10-08",
      "speech_order": "361",
      "word_count": 4380,
      "classification_status": "classified",
      "text_preview": "Those opposite do not like when I compare what is happening here with the place where they are in government. We are also taking an important step towards removing the means tests for our carers. A big move was made yest"
    },
    {
      "rank": 6,
      "member_code": "Jennifer-Carroll-MacNeill.D.2020-02-08",
      "full_name": "Jennifer Carroll MacNeill",
      "speech_id": "speech:79f459ed17bdec7d6b9c4c7a",
      "debate_date": "2026-06-18",
      "speech_order": "297",
      "word_count": 4316,
      "classification_status": "classified",
      "text_preview": "I begin not with policy, but with people. I acknowledge with sincerity and respect the people across Ireland who are living with a rare disease and the parents, partners, children, siblings, carers, families and friends "
    },
    {
      "rank": 7,
      "member_code": "Thomas-Byrne.D.2007-06-14",
      "full_name": "Thomas Byrne",
      "speech_id": "speech:367b82417f3061f1f35a684b",
      "debate_date": "2026-05-07",
      "speech_order": "289",
      "word_count": 4257,
      "classification_status": "classified",
      "text_preview": "Is mór an onóir dom labhairt sa Dáil inniu ar ócáid Lá na hEorpa. As Minister of State with responsibility for European affairs, I am proud to speak today to mark Europe Day. In less than eight weeks' time, on 1 July 202"
    },
    {
      "rank": 8,
      "member_code": "Jennifer-Carroll-MacNeill.D.2020-02-08",
      "full_name": "Jennifer Carroll MacNeill",
      "speech_id": "speech:82d00fdc09346e79177dfe4a",
      "debate_date": "2025-04-29",
      "speech_order": "290",
      "word_count": 4249,
      "classification_status": "classified",
      "text_preview": "We are here today because the HIQA review has laid bare significant failures at Children’s Health Ireland, failures that I believe have put children at risk of harm. Children who deserved the very highest standards of ca"
    },
    {
      "rank": 9,
      "member_code": "Mary-Butler.D.2016-10-03",
      "full_name": "Mary Butler",
      "speech_id": "speech:b5dda091deda6139fda11ae3",
      "debate_date": "2025-02-18",
      "speech_order": "305",
      "word_count": 4138,
      "classification_status": "classified",
      "text_preview": "I thank the Cathaoirleach for the opportunity to discuss the important topic of mental health today. It is fitting that mental health is one of the first themes for Dáil statements of this Government's term. It highlight"
    },
    {
      "rank": 10,
      "member_code": "Simon-Harris.D.2011-03-09",
      "full_name": "Simon Harris",
      "speech_id": "speech:062e3b7456048ecee54e934a",
      "debate_date": "2025-10-01",
      "speech_order": "150",
      "word_count": 4120,
      "classification_status": "classified",
      "text_preview": "I have just returned in recent days from the UN high-level week in New York, where the Middle East was a central focus of my agenda. This is a timely debate as we assess the horrendous situation in Gaza and the West Bank"
    }
